.\" Manpage for senbonzakura.
.TH SENBONZAKURA 1 "2026-09-17" "senbonzakura 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
senbonzakura \- refusal abliteration for transformer language models, with the
instruments to measure what the edit cost
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B senbonzakura
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-track
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-trials
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-directions
.IR K ]
.RB [ \-\-search
.IR pareto | scalar ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B senbonzakura kageyoshi
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-out
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-track
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR cuda | cpu ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B senbonzakura
removes the refusal behaviour from an open weight language model by finding the
.I directions
in its activation space that carry "I can't help with that" and orthogonalising
them out of the residual writing weights. It builds on the single direction method
of Arditi et al. and the automated search of Heretic, and can ablate more than one
direction per layer.
.PP
.B Whether more than one helps is not established, and this tool does not claim it.
An earlier version of this page said that cutting several directions at once clears the
residual refusal at no cost to coherence. That claim was tested and withdrawn:
across five seeds a side, two directions cost roughly 1.5 to 1.9 times the collateral
damage of one at the same refusal rate (permutation p = 0.016). Those arms were
selected by a filter since found to accept every candidate it was shown, so the
honest reading is narrower still: what was measured is that
.I arbitrary
second directions cost drift, and the question has not been answered in either
direction under the extractor shipping today. Left to itself the search picks one
direction more often than not. See
.B senbonzakura validate
for the commands that ask the question.
.PP
The method has three stages. First, per layer refusal directions are extracted:
the good orthogonalised difference of means, plus secondary axes from clustered
difference of means over the harmful residual cloud, giving an orthonormal basis of
the candidate subspace. A held out separation filter is applied to each candidate
against a measured null direction floor.
Second, an Optuna search (NSGA\-II by default) explores a windowed, per component,
multi\-directional ablation and scores each candidate by applying the real,
norm preserving weight bake, so the search optimises the exact model it will save.
The search minimises three objectives at once: strict non\-compliance (hard refusal
plus hedging), the Heretic keyword rate, and KL divergence from the original model
on harmless prompts (the coherence guard). Third, the winning configuration is
baked permanently into the weights and saved.
.SH BANKAI MODE
.TP
.B senbonzakura kageyoshi
Ultimate balanced\-effort abliteration with no manual tuning. It detects the
architecture (dense, fused MoE, or expert list) and parameter count, scales the
search budget to the model's size, and enables every quality lever: the three
objective NSGA\-II front with knee selection, the multi\-direction refusal subspace,
the larger\-eval knee re\-score, and early stop. If a
.I hedge_ds
directory is present in the track directory, the hedging contrast direction is
folded in automatically. The mode is deliberately balanced, it selects the most
uncensored configuration that remains coherent (guarded by the KL ceiling and the
coherence penalty), not the most aggressive one. Only the path and device flags are
honoured; the search budget flags are managed internally and ignored in this mode.
.SH KEY OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-model " DIR"
Path to the base model to abliterate.
.TP
.BI \-\-out " DIR"
Where to write the abliterated model and
.IR abliteration.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-track " DIR"
Directory holding the datasets:
.IR bad_ds ", " good_ds ", " bad_eval_ds .
.TP
.BI \-\-trials " N"
Number of Optuna search trials (default 60).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-directions " K"
Upper bound on refusal directions ablated per layer. 1 is the original single
direction method; greater than 1 enables the multi\-direction subspace ablation.
.TP
.BI \-\-search " pareto|scalar"
.B pareto
maps the whole frontier with NSGA\-II and picks the knee afterwards;
.B scalar
uses a single weighted objective with TPE.
.TP
.BI \-\-kl\-scale " F"
Weight on KL in the scalar objective. Higher protects quality harder.
.TP
.B \-\-per\-component
Tune attention o_proj and MLP down_proj separately (the default). The MLP profile
may fall to zero, leaving the MLP untouched, which often preserves intelligence.
.TP
.B \-\-mlp\-off
Attention only: pin the MLP ablation to zero and drop its search dimensions. Tests
the "attention carries refusal, MLP carries capability" hypothesis.
.TP
.BI \-\-hedge\-ds " DIR"
A hedged compliance dataset (moralising but complying answers). When given, a
hedged versus clean contrast direction is folded into the ablated basis, so the
search can strip the disclaimer axis the difference of means direction misses.
.TP
.BI \-\-patience " N"
Stop the search early once no trial improves the best score for N consecutive
trials (0 runs all trials).
.TP
.BI \-\-eval\-refusal\-final " N"
Re\-score the top frontier candidates on N bad\-eval prompts before picking the
knee, so the choice is not overfit to the small search eval.
.TP
.BI \-\-inspect " LAYER STRENGTH"
Print real harmful and harmless generations at one (layer, strength), before and
after ablation, then exit. Use it to see whether high KL means "wrecked" or just
"a few benign first tokens flipped".
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Bankai, the no\-tuning best effort (recommended):
.PP
.RS
.nf
senbonzakura kageyoshi \-\-model ./base \-\-track ./ds \-\-out ./abliterated
.fi
.RE
.PP
A multi\-direction Pareto search, 200 trials, with the larger knee re\-score:
.PP
.RS
.nf
senbonzakura \-\-model ./base \-\-track ./ds \-\-out ./abliterated \\
    \-\-search pareto \-\-max\-directions 6 \-\-trials 200 \\
    \-\-eval\-refusal\-final 256 \-\-patience 40
.fi
.RE
.PP
Attention only ablation with a hedged contrast:
.PP
.RS
.nf
senbonzakura \-\-model ./base \-\-track ./ds \-\-out ./att \\
    \-\-mlp\-off \-\-hedge\-ds ./ds/hedged_ds \-\-max\-directions 4
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a clean early exit from
.BR \-\-inspect / \-\-bench\-only .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
These change what a run does or what it records, and none of them has a flag.
.TP
.B HF_TOKEN
Hugging Face access token, used for gated or private models and datasets.
.B HUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN
is read as a fallback, and the Hub's own stored login after that. Prefer either
variable over the
.B \-\-hf\-token
flag: an argument is visible to anyone who can run
.BR ps (1).
.TP
.B SENBONZAKURA_COMMIT
The commit to record in a run's provenance when
.BR git (1)
cannot answer, which is the case on a rented pod or an unpacked tarball rather
than a checkout. A
.B CODE_VERSION
file beside the package or at the tree root is read first and is the better
option, because a file travels with the tree while a variable has to be
remembered at launch. Write it with
.RS
.nf

git rev\-parse \-\-short HEAD > CODE_VERSION

.fi
.RE
With neither, the run records no commit at all, and a result that cannot say
which code produced it is not reproducible.
.TP
.B SENBONZAKURA_TRACK_BACKEND
Pins the table backend used to read and write evaluation tracks:
.IR auto " (default), " pyarrow " or " datasets .
A value that is not one of those is refused rather than ignored.
.TP
.B SENBON_RUN_ISOLATED
Absolute path to
.IR headtohead/run\-isolated.sh ,
for a machine where the benchmark runs from an installed wheel rather than a
checkout. Only affects
.BR "senbonzakura head\-to\-head" .
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Where the bundled evaluation track is unpacked, as
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME/senbonzakura/bundled\-track ,
so by default
.IR ~/.cache/senbonzakura/bundled\-track .
That directory is the track itself, and it is what to point
.B senbonzakura track \-\-audit \-\-out
at in order to check it.
.B senbonzakura doctor
prints the resolved path beside the track's size.
.SH ACCEPTABLE USE
A model that has been through this tool will answer requests the original
refused, including harmful ones. That is what it does, and everything here
follows from it.
.PP
Do not put an abliterated model in front of other people without saying what it
is: the people using it cannot see the weights and have no way to know the
refusals are gone. Do not use it to produce material that is illegal where you
are; removing a model's refusals does not make its output lawful. Do not use it
against a model you are not permitted to modify.
.PP
Three licences are usually in play and they do not merge. This software is
AGPL\-3.0\-or\-later. The base model keeps its own licence, because abliteration
is a modification and not a relicensing, and several model families carry a use
policy that binds derivatives. The bundled corpora carry their own terms: the
evaluation track is CC BY\-NC 4.0, attribution required and non\-commercial.
.PP
The package carries roughly 6,500 harmful prompts so it can run with no network.
They are prompts and not answers, they are obfuscated only to keep them out of
automated scrapes, and one ordinary run unpacks them to your cache directory in
plain form. On a shared machine, consider whether whoever administers it would
expect that.
.PP
The full text is
.B ACCEPTABLE\-USE.md ,
installed beside the package under its dist\-info/licenses/ directory.
